      "description": "Watch Belgrano Cordoba vs Argentinos JRS highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 1, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina clash between Belgrano and Argentinos JRS on August 1st, 2026 , proved to be a high-stakes tactical battle defined by disciplinary drama and a clinical finish. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish dominance, but the match would eventually pivot on a single moment of madness and a perfectly timed strike. Red Card Drama and the Breakthrough The first half was characterized by rising tension that boiled over in the 37th minute. Franco Vazquez , who had already been cautioned with a yellow card ten minutes earlier, saw red after a controversial challenge. His dismissal sparked heavy protests from the Belgrano squad, but the referee remained unmoved, forcing the hosts to navigate the remainder of the contest with only ten men. The numerical advantage quickly emboldened the visitors. As the clock ticked deep into first-half stoppage time, Argentinos JRS made their breakthrough. In the 45+3rd minute, Cesar Florentin provided a pinpoint assist for Francisco Alvarez , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. It was a devastating blow for Belgrano , coming just seconds before the half-time whistle, and it completely altered the complexion of the game heading into the break. Tactical Adjustments and the Final Stand Both managers looked to their benches to start the second half. Belgrano introduced Santiago Longo and Lucas Passerini in an attempt to stabilize their formation, while Argentinos JRS brought on Emiliano Viveros . The second period was a gritty affair, with both teams fighting for every inch of grass. The physical nature of the contest continued to manifest in the referee's notebook, as Tomas Molina received a yellow card in the 54th minute for a mistimed challenge. A flurry of late substitutions defined the closing stages as fatigue set in. Argentinos JRS managed their lead effectively, introducing fresh legs like Matias Gimenez Rojas and Claudio Bravo . Despite Belgrano's best efforts to find an equalizer through late substitutes Ramiro Tulian and Lautaro Gutierrez , the visitors held firm. The final whistle after seven minutes of added time confirmed a hard-fought victory for Argentinos JRS , leaving the home fans to rue the early dismissal."
